{"id": "EUVD-2026-86737", "enisaUuid": "9f16ca1d-9df8-32dd-8c06-fdb54fbe2dbb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfs: autofs: fix memory leak in autofs_fill_super()\n\nIn autofs_fill_super(), we create a new inode using\nautofs_new_ino(), however, if we fail to create root_inode,\n(that is, root_inode failure path), we return -ENOMEM without\nfreeing the new inode(ino) that we created causing a memory leak.\nFix this by adding autofs_free_ino() to free the inode we created\nin root_inode failure path before returning ENOMEM.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:10:10", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4262b91e08e74cb5209ea737c554cf983d332382", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9933ad1c4ff67680cd59c47f6d2e81b533bcd467", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6259b5d9bdc45fdb3158406b28c27fa074823159", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ab54837fce04a1c9923d0bfd3d5de51fdc768b3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97606", "GHSA-658w-8mcr-xc7q"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "181f0730-9b0a-3e55-96bb-3f595ca60873", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "2aa9f0cb-ae05-3cff-9fda-c75ad9c7c96c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3eda89ed-5831-3d46-82b3-b3e9ecb3a79d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66917f85db6002ed09cd24186258892fcfca64b6 <9933ad1c4ff67680cd59c47f6d2e81b533bcd467"}, {"id": "42d5b5f7-74db-321a-a84b-c7c50cd5c09f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66917f85db6002ed09cd24186258892fcfca64b6 <5ab54837fce04a1c9923d0bfd3d5de51fdc768b3"}, {"id": "43b2eea5-2401-39d6-8be3-1e7b03505fe1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "66917f85db6002ed09cd24186258892fcfca64b6 <6259b5d9bdc45fdb